--- 3. [RETRACTED 2026-11-15: this section's conclusion is false.  The four failures do occur, and not from these caches; see section 6.  The probe results below stand.] ---
probe, base tree: cones of `projective_space_fan()` and of `hirzebruch_surface_fan(0)`
over one `ZZ.free_module(2)` that have the same rays
  same rays [(0, 1), (1, 0)]   eq: False   hash eq: True   engine cones eq: True
  same rays [(0, 1), (1, 0)]   eq: False   hash eq: True   engine cones eq: False
`fans.py:751` requires `element_parent(other) is self.parent()` for cone equality, while
`fans.py:95` hashes the ray coordinates, so equal-cone cache hits happen only inside one
fan object.  Inside one fan the equal copies are `c.intersection(c)`, `C.faces(k)` members
and pairwise intersections of maximal cones; over P2, P1xP1, Hirzebruch 2, the A1 cone and
P3 the Hilbert basis came back in the same order from every copy, 0 disagreements out of
every pair tested.

[RETRACTED: the sentence that followed -- that "the base tree has no failing instance to
observe and the repair is the invariant, not a reproduced red" -- is false.  It was drawn
from runs of the file alone.  Run in one process after two `tests/sets` files, the same
tree fails four of the file's seven tests, and the cause is the augmentation identity of
the chart's free algebra, not these caches.  Section 6 records the reproduction.]

