6b. the minimal reproduction, algebra-only, on the base tree
  QQ.polynomial_ring("y")
  algebra = AffineSemigroupAlgebras(QQ)(((1, 0), (0, 1)),)
  algebra.Mor(algebra).identity()
-> ValueError: the whole-algebra map for Free module on Coproduct of the family over NN over
   Fraction Field of Integer Ring has different endpoints Multivariate Polynomial Ring in
   s0, s1 over Rational Field -> Multivariate Polynomial Ring in s0, s1 over Rational Field
   (algebras.py:4645, from PresentedAlgebraMorphism.__init__, from
   _AlgebraMorCommonMethods._from_engine_morphism :4789, from PresentedAlgebraMor.identity
   :4893, from the augmentation at :5254, from selected_resolution :938, from
   algebra_generator :2057, from toric_schemes.py:262)
Without the polynomial ring first the same three lines pass: the identity is built and fixes
the generator.  With it, two different answers for one algebra.

6c. why: the arrow class is decided by the order of the parent classes, not by the algebra
`AlgebrasWithChosenFinitePresentation.ParentMethods._algebra_mor_class` (algebras.py:3547)
and `FreeAlgebras.ParentMethods._algebra_mor_class` (free_algebras.py:1580) both answer for a
semigroup algebra on a free monoid -- it is the polynomial algebra and a finitely presented
algebra at once.  Which one is reached is the MRO of the object's generated `_with_category`
class, and that order follows what was built before:
  without QQ[y]  MRO: ... GradedAlgebras.ParentMethods, FreeAlgebras.ParentMethods,
                       _CommutativeUnitalAlgebraParentMethods,
                       AlgebrasWithChosenFinitePresentation.ParentMethods ...
                 answer: FramedFreeAlgebraMor   (identity builds from generator images)
  with QQ[y]     MRO: ... GradedAlgebras.ParentMethods,
                       AlgebrasWithChosenFinitePresentation.ParentMethods,
                       FreeAlgebras.ParentMethods ...
                 answer: PresentedAlgebraMor     (identity goes through the engine ring)
Deterministic per construction history and independent of PYTHONHASHSEED: eight runs without
QQ[y] answered FramedFreeAlgebraMor eight times, three with it answered PresentedAlgebraMor
three times.  `PresentedAlgebraMor.identity` builds `engine.hom(engine)` and
`PresentedAlgebraMorphism` refuses it, so the augmentation of the free algebra's own
degree-zero resolution -- the one arrow that must exist before the resolution is installed --
is built in a class that cannot build it.

6d. the repair
`AlgebrasWithChosenFinitePresentation.ParentMethods._algebra_mor_class` defers to
`FreeAlgebras.ParentMethods._algebra_mor_class` when the algebra is a free algebra, so the
answer is a function of the algebra rather than of the parent-class order, and the identity
is built by the class that can build it (generator images, no engine arrow, no
`module_category` of the algebra, which does not exist yet at that point).
The caches of the first turn stay keyed by the cone's value, and `_semigroup_generator_positions`
became `AffineSemigroupAlgebras.affine_semigroup_generator_positions` -- a datum of the algebra,
which already carried `affine_semigroup_generator_coordinates`.

